  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The electromagnetic (EM) spectrum is the range of all types of EM radiation. The&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>&#8208;</mo></math>ray&nbsp;has a maximum frequency or minimum wavelength; since the wavelength is inversely proportional to frequency, while radio wave&nbsp;has a minimum frequency and maximum wavelength. The order of wavelength will be;&nbsp;Gamma rays&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>G</mi></math> &lt; X-rays <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>&nbsp;&lt; Ultra violet&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>U</mi></math> &lt; Visible rays&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math> &lt; Infrared rays&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi></math> &lt; Microwaves&nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math>&nbsp;&lt; Radio waves <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>.</p></blockquote>",
